{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.StokesJump","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.StokesJump","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.PhragmenLindelof","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Gaussian.GaussianIntegral","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.BorelWatson","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.BorelWatsonUniqueness"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.stokesJump_beyondAllOrders","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.stokesJump_beyondAllOrders","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/StokesJump.lean#L94-L134","doc":"**A Stokes jump is beyond all orders.**  If `‖jump x‖ ≤ C·exp(−b·x^s)` with\n`b > 0`, `s > 1`, then `x^N·‖jump x‖ → 0` for **every** real `N` — the jump\ndecays faster than any power of `x`.\n\nThis is the reason alien calculus exists.  A formal asymptotic series in\n`x^{-1}` sees only the powers; a term killed by every power is invisible to\nit.  So two functions with the *same* asymptotic expansion can differ by a\nStokes jump, the expansion cannot distinguish them, and the alien derivative\nis the invariant that can.  `gevrey_difference_stokesJumpBound` above supplies\nthe hypothesis from a Gevrey-1 remainder bound; this consumes it.\n\nNote `C ≥ 0` is not assumed — it follows, since `‖jump x‖ ≥ 0` and the\nexponential is positive wherever the bound holds.\n\nReplaces a `: True := trivial` placeholder that carried the docstring \"the\nStokes jump at a singular Borel ray equals the alien derivative data\" while\nconcluding nothing (AGENTS.md §1a).  That equality is the bridge equation and\nis *not* proved here; this is the one-directional fact the file's own\nmachinery does establish.  Nothing in the corpus referenced the placeholder.\n\n-- Ref: [ecalle1981] Fonctions résurgentes, tome I\n-- Ref: [sauzin2014] https://arxiv.org/abs/1405.0356 ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.gevrey_difference_stokesJumpBound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.gevrey_difference_stokesJumpBound","kind":"theorem","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/StokesJump.lean#L33-L92","doc":"Gevrey-1 remainder bound implies Stokes jump bound.\n\n**Proof.** Apply `gevrey1_remainder_expDecay` with ε = x^{−s}, giving\n`‖jump x‖ ≤ C·e²·√(x^s)·exp(−x^s)`. Then `√(x^s) ≤ exp(x^s/2)` by\n`sqrt_le_exp_half`, so `‖jump x‖ ≤ C·e²·exp(−x^s/2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.StokesJumpBound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.StokesJumpBound","kind":"def","line":17,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/StokesJump.lean#L17-L19","doc":"A Stokes jump satisfies `|jump(x)| ≤ C·exp(−b·x^s)` for `s > 1, b > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.StokesJump.sumRight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.StokesJump.sumRight","kind":"def","line":15,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/StokesJump.lean#L15-L15","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.StokesJump.sumLeft","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.StokesJump.sumLeft","kind":"def","line":14,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/StokesJump.lean#L14-L14","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.StokesJump.theta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.StokesJump.theta","kind":"def","line":13,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/StokesJump.lean#L13-L13","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.StokesJump.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.StokesJump.mk","kind":"ctor","line":12,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/StokesJump.lean#L12-L12","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.StokesJump","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.StokesJump","kind":"structure","line":11,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/StokesJump.lean#L11-L15","doc":"A Stokes jump at angle θ is the difference of two directional Borel sums. ","signatureChunk":0}]}